*(mgec-activities2006
<div id="sitemap_content" style="width:500px">
  <table CELLPADDING=6 CELLSPACING=4 BORDER=0 WIDTH=700>
    <tr>
      <td WIDTH="100%" VALIGN="TOP">
        <p style="margin-bottom: 8px;">
          <span style="font-family: Verdana, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 120%; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 6px;">
            Maize Genetics Executive Committee: Activities, 2006
          </span>
        </p>
        <br>
        <p>
         Worked with the National Corn Growers Association (NCGA\) to help them 
         communicate the importance of maize genome sequence to scientists and 
         farmers. 
        </p>
        <br>
        <p>
          Developed a survey (<a href="/docs/SurveyResults06.doc">results</a>\) that 
          went to all maize genetics community members. Synthesized the survey 
          and posted results on maizeGDB. The results were also sent to funding 
          agencies and NCGA. 
        </p>
        <br>
        <p>
          Members of the committee, Ed Buckler and Jo Messing spoke at the Post 
          Maize Genome Sequence meeting for NCGA (August 2006\)
        </p>
        <br>
        <p>
          Initiated plans for a new comprehensive Maize Handbook (Jeff 
          Bennetzen and Sarah Hake, editors\)
        </p>
        <br>
        <p><i>Contributed by Sarah Hake</i></p>
        
        <br>
        
        <p>
          <a href="/mgec">Maize Genetics Executive Committee</a><br>
          <a href="/">MaizeGDB Homepage</a>
        </p>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</div>
)